PLAN=plan(9,'Perimeter, area, surface area and volume','Part IV · Shape, structure and measure',16,'Globalization and sustainability','Measurement, Space','Choosing the right measure—length, area, surface area or volume—connects geometric structure to material use, capacity and cost.','How can a community project estimate turf, paving, fencing, soil and paint without confusing boundary, surface and space?','In order for a student to apply mathematics in real-life contexts, students must select the correct measure, convert units, calculate costs and evaluate a budget with stated assumptions.',S,explore,application,assessment,mixed,ready,check,[S[0]['diagram'],S[1]['diagram'],S[2]['diagram'],S[3]['diagram']],['Distinguish perimeter, area, surface area and volume.','Calculate with triangles, quadrilaterals, circles and composites.','Use nets and prism formulas with correct units.','Convert capacity, compare packaging and evaluate a project budget.'],'perimeter · area · surface area · volume · capacity · radius · diameter · circumference · semicircle · composite · net · prism · cross-section · litre',key='Form',sourcepages='174–193; answers 234–237')
